//! flags: -p canonicalize

// An internal error must unwind rather than abort().
//
// ErrorReport's destructor used to call abort() with its `throw` commented
// out, which made cli::run()'s `catch (const Error &)` unreachable. Because
// the test runner compiles in-process, that abort took the whole runner down
// before it could record anything -- which is why every test in this
// directory failed at the time, with the harness reporting "Subprocess
// aborted" and no captured output at all.
//
// So what this pins down is the *shape* of a failure, not this particular
// diagnostic: exit code 1, with the message on stderr and printed exactly
// once. The error below is raised while building the IR for the expression,
// so there are real frames to unwind through. Set BONSAI_ABORT_ON_ERROR to
// get the old aborting behaviour back under a debugger.
func f(a : f32, b : bool) -> f32 {
    return a + b;
}
